            <div xml:id="d64">

                <pb facs="0157" n="67" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg67"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.73/14: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-11-13T13:00:00-05:29"><hi rendition="#italic">November 13,
                                1920—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received (?):24
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>298. The Western Union Company has laid no cable under the permit granted by the
                    Cuban Government, but is making preparations <pb facs="0158" n="68"
                        xml:id="pg68"/> to do so. No cable connection has been made from any place
                    near Miami with Habana. I am making further investigations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
